[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-GRAMMAR-CANNOT-SPELL-THE-VOCABULARY
TITLE: The grammar cannot spell the ruled vocabulary
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
PLACE: screen
STATEMENT: >>>
Six ruled types are absent from the grammar and three grammar types are dissolved. Because a UID's prefix spells its type, every retype mints a new UID. The migration is uncosted, has no work node, and waits on the plan-lifecycle decision — which retires only after a plan finishes under a beads that does not yet run.

> The grammar cannot spell the ruled vocabulary: REQUIREMENT|USE CASE|EVIDENCE|WORK|NARRATIVE|PLAN absent, SLICE|INVARIANT|SPIKE dissolved, UID prefixes carry type so every retype re-mints UIDs; the migration is uncosted, has no WORK node, and is gated on DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN, which retires only after a plan finishes under a beads that does not run.

Since the sheet: the ruled types entered the grammar on 2026-08-30 and every node was retyped in place under [LINK: DEC-NODE-FAMILIES], each keeping its UID under [LINK: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE]; the wait on [LINK: DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN] did not hold. PLAN alone is still absent from the grammar.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
